Bug: .github/workflows/vendorapp-ci.yml "print/debugPrint/log sweep" step
self-fails on this ticket's own diff.

Repro (run from VendorApp/ in the NEARS-812 worktree, exact command copied
from the workflow file):

  hits="$(grep -rnE '(^|[^a-zA-Z_])(print|debugPrint|log)\(' lib/features/ --include='*.dart' \
    | grep -v '^lib/features/store/screens/store_edit_screen.dart:.*log(' \
    | grep -v '^lib/features/store/domain/repositories/store_repository.dart:' \
    | grep -v '^lib/features/payment/screens/payment_screen.dart:' \
    | grep -v '^lib/features/auth/domain/repositories/auth_repository.dart:.*Device Token' || true)"
  if [ -n "$hits" ]; then
    echo "FAIL: raw print()/debugPrint()/log() found in lib/features/** — route through AppLogger instead."
    echo "$hits"
    exit 1
  fi

Actual output:
  FAIL: raw print()/debugPrint()/log() found in lib/features/** — route through AppLogger instead.
  lib/features/auth/domain/repositories/auth_repository.dart:1:// NEARS-812: intentionally-retained device-token print() outside this ticket's scope (NEARS-807/820); NEARS-840 tracks removal.

Root cause: auth_repository.dart's own new top-of-file explanatory comment
(added by this ticket) contains the literal substring "print()" (lowercase
"device-token", not "Device Token"). The file's exclusion filter only
matches lines containing the exact substring "Device Token" (capitalized),
so it does not exclude this comment line, and the grep step exits 1.

Impact: this CI job will go red on the very commit that introduces it (and
on every subsequent PR touching this file), defeating the purpose of Scope
(in)'s "add the CI grep gate" deliverable. Verified independently that the
underlying detection logic is otherwise sound — a genuinely injected
debugPrint()/log() into a scratch lib/features/**/*.dart file IS correctly
caught (confirmed separately, not a detection-logic defect, just this one
exclusion filter being too narrow / comment-sensitive).

Fix suggestion: either reword the comment to avoid the literal substrings
print(/debugPrint(/log(, or (more robust) exclude auth_repository.dart's
comment/import header lines by line number the same way the CI gate already
whole-file-excludes payment_screen.dart and store_repository.dart, instead
of a content-substring filter that only matches "Device Token".
